WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.987
Adam was going to work with Mom for the day.

2
00:00:04.988 --> 00:00:08.885
"Delivering mail will be fun," said Adam.

3
00:00:08.886 --> 00:00:14.498
"A lot more fun than learning stuff at school."

4
00:00:14.499 --> 00:00:19.422
"You're going to work hard," said Mom.

5
00:00:19.423 --> 00:00:24.600
"And you'll still be learning—all about helping customers."

6
00:00:24.601 --> 00:00:33.265
"That sounds better than learning about fractions!" said Adam.

7
00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:40.057
At the post office, Adam and Mom filled two large mailbags.

8
00:00:40.058 --> 00:00:49.276
Then they drove to a busy neighborhood to deliver the letters and packages.

9
00:00:49.277 --> 00:00:52.392
Adam wiped sweat from his forehead.

10
00:00:52.393 --> 00:00:58.057
"My mailbag is so heavy. When's morning recess?"

11
00:00:58.058 --> 00:01:00.812
Mom chuckled.

12
00:01:00.813 --> 00:01:04.763
"There's no recess when you're working!" she said.

13
00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:08.186
"But later we'll take a short lunch break."

14
00:01:08.187 --> 00:01:13.170
She pointed up a steep hill. "Follow me!"

15
00:01:13.171 --> 00:01:18.025
At the top of the hill, Adam carried a package to a house.

16
00:01:18.026 --> 00:01:23.866
"Woof! Woof!" A dog barked from inside.

17
00:01:23.867 --> 00:01:28.582
"Shh, Peanut!" said a woman.

18
00:01:28.583 --> 00:01:34.660
She opened the door wider to get her mail—and the dog dashed outside.

19
00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:39.371
"Oh no! My precious Peanut!" cried the woman.

20
00:01:39.372 --> 00:01:44.339
Peanut charged after a garbage truck.

21
00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:48.991
"I'll get him!" Adam yelled, running after the dog.

22
00:01:48.992 --> 00:01:55.314
They raced down the hill.

23
00:01:55.315 --> 00:02:02.525
Peanut chased a butterfly and a skateboarder.

24
00:02:02.526 --> 00:02:07.434
Finally he stopped to sniff a fire hydrant.

25
00:02:07.435 --> 00:02:10.635
Adam pounced. "Gotcha!"

26
00:02:10.636 --> 00:02:19.577
When Adam came back with Peanut, he was huffing and puffing.

27
00:02:19.578 --> 00:02:25.604
"Good job," Mom said. "Now back to work!"

28
00:02:25.605 --> 00:02:32.043
Adam groaned and followed his mother.

29
00:02:32.044 --> 00:02:36.023
Their last delivery was on Chestnut Street.

30
00:02:36.024 --> 00:02:41.623
Adam started to put letters into the mailbox.

31
00:02:41.624 --> 00:02:45.285
A man stomped angrily toward them.

32
00:02:45.286 --> 00:02:49.621
"My mail is late!" he growled.

33
00:02:49.622 --> 00:02:52.931
"I've been waiting all afternoon!"

34
00:02:52.932 --> 00:02:58.659
"Very sorry, sir!" said Mom politely.

35
00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:02.239
Adam and Mom drove back to the post office.

36
00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:06.529
"That man was rude, Mom."

37
00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:07.686
Mom shrugged.

38
00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:10.130
"Mail carriers have to be polite.

39
00:03:10.131 --> 00:03:16.994
That's a big part of the job."

40
00:03:16.995 --> 00:03:22.116
At home Adam fell onto the sofa. "Phew!"

41
00:03:22.117 --> 00:03:25.638
"Tired?" asked Mom.

42
00:03:25.639 --> 00:03:28.540
"Yes!" said Adam.

43
00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:36.708
"Working was fun, but I can't wait to get back to school!"

